  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The Bloodroot Poison gets into the bloodstream and causes a very gradual internal necrosis. A creature that ingests this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 7 (2d6) poison damage and become poisoned. The poisoned creature must repeat the saving throw every 24 hours, taking 7 (2d6) poison damage on a failed save.</p>\n<p>Until this poison ends, the damage the poison deals can’t be healed by any means. After seven successful saving throws, the effect ends and the creature can heal normally.</p>",
